    "result_text": "Full suite is green \u2014 **38 tests, 0 failures**, including the two new `Cp27Tests`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is a read-time derived value on the owner response, so I implemented it the same way the codebase handles its other derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`) \u2014 via the OpenAPI schema plus a MapStruct mapping expression.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` schema (readOnly string, `enum: [EMAIL, PHONE]`). The build's openapi-generator turns this into a nested `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` deriving the value:\n   ```java\n   (owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank())\n       ? ContactPreferenceEnum.EMAIL : ContactPreferenceEnum.PHONE\n   ```\n\nBecause the GET response flows through `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, every owner read now returns `contactPreference = EMAIL` when an email is present and `PHONE` otherwise. The blank-string guard matches the convention the existing `membershipLevel` rule already uses for \"email present.\"",
